    <div class="list">
      <!-- FAQ 1 -->
      <div class="q open">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-1">
            How does a custom Salowtech CRM differ from SaaS tools like Salesforce or HubSpot?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-1">
          <div>
            <p>
              Off-the-shelf SaaS platforms lock your business into steep recurring per-user monthly subscription fees
              and force your workflow into their rigid templates. A Salowtech custom CRM is built around your exact
              sales pipeline, eliminates per-seat licensing fees forever, and runs on your sovereign infrastructure.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 2 -->
      <div class="q">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-2">
            Can our custom CRM integrate with WhatsApp, email, telephony, and accounting systems?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-2">
          <div>
            <p>
              Yes. We integrate official WhatsApp Business Cloud API, two-way email tracking (Gmail/Outlook), VoIP
              telephony (Twilio, Exotel) for click-to-call recording, and automatic invoice sync with Tally, QuickBooks,
              or Zoho Books.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 3 -->
      <div class="q">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-3">
            How does the CRM help sales teams close deals faster?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-3">
          <div>
            <p>
              Our CRM features intelligent lead scoring, automated task reminders, interactive Kanban deal boards,
              real-time quote generation, and automated follow-up drip sequences that ensure no high-value opportunity
              slips through the cracks.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 4 -->
      <div class="q">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-4">
            What security measures protect our client contact list and deal financials?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-4">
          <div>
            <p>
              Your client data is protected by granular Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), preventing reps from exporting
              or viewing records outside their assigned territory. All database tables are encrypted with AES-256,
              backed by immutable audit logs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 5 -->
      <div class="q">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-5">
            How long does custom CRM deployment take, and how do we migrate existing data?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-5">
          <div>
            <p>
              An operational MVP CRM deploys in 4 to 8 weeks. We provide zero-downtime ETL migration scripts that clean,
              deduplicate, and import your existing customer records from legacy spreadsheets, Salesforce, or Zoho
              without disruption.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ 6 -->
      <div class="q">
        <h3>
          <button type="button" id="faq-crm-btn-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-crm-ans-6">
            Do we own the full source code and data after launch?
            <i class="ic" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        </h3>
        <div class="a" id="faq-crm-ans-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-crm-btn-6">
          <div>
            <p>
              Yes. You hold 100% intellectual property ownership of the code, database, and configurations. You can host
              it on your private cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP) or on-premise servers with total autonomy.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

